[0.45, "o", "Title:      \u001b[1mShip Hybrid Local Remote And SSH Execution\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:     \u001b[1m\u001b[92mverified\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\r\nArchetype:  \u001b[95m\u001b[1mStrategic\u001b[0m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-01\u001b[0m - Convert bearing VDcStPolu into executable board work for hybrid local, remote, cloud, and SSH-first execution. (\u001b[2mVDcStPolu\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-02\u001b[0m - Keep the mission surfaces doctor-clean and make this hybrid-execution mission visible through the board command surfaces. (\u001b[2mrun `just keel mission show VDesj389j`, `just flow`, and `just keel doctor`\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mChildren\u001b[0m\r\n  Epics (1):\r\n    \u001b[1m\u001b[36mVDcStPolu\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - Hybrid Local Remote And SSH Execution (\u001b[2mdone\u001b[0m)\r\n  Bearings (1):\r\n    \u001b[1m\u001b[94mVDcStPolu\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - Hybrid Local Remote And SSH Execution (\u001b[2mlaid\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mLatest Log Entry\u001b[0m\r\n    2026-03-12T06:12:53\r\n"]
[1.8, "o", "$ sed -n '1,120p' .keel/missions/VDesj389j/CHARTER.md\r\n"]
[2.25, "o", "# Ship Hybrid Local Remote And SSH Execution - Charter\r\n\r\n## Goals\r\n\r\n| ID | Description | Verification |\r\n|----|-------------|--------------|\r\n| MG-01 | Convert bearing VDcStPolu into executable board work for hybrid local, remote, cloud, and SSH-first execution. | board: VDcStPolu |\r\n| MG-02 | Keep the mission surfaces doctor-clean and make this hybrid-execution mission visible through the board command surfaces. | manual: run `just keel mission show VDesj389j`, `just flow`, and `just keel doctor` |\r\n\r\n## Constraints\r\n\r\n- Keep one canonical `port` CLI and guest vocabulary across local, hosted, and SSH-owned execution instead of introducing a separate remote-only command surface.\r\n- Use bearing VDcStPolu plus the existing hosted, cloud, and operator artifacts as the primary sources, and do not broaden scope into storage normalization, k3s, or GPU work unless the hybrid contract requires explicit downstream follow-up.\r\n- Preserve the hard-cutover policy: do not add compatibility aliases or dual operator paths just to bridge old and new remote-execution semantics.\r\n\r\n## Halting Rules\r\n\r\n- DO NOT halt while any MG-* goal has unfinished board work\r\n- HALT when the hybrid execution work is decomposed into executable board items and only verification-oriented manual checks remain\r\n- YIELD to human when prioritization depends on provider choice, SSH trust model, or remote bootstrap assumptions that are not inferable from the repository\r\n"]
[3.6, "o", "$ keel epic show VDcStPolu\r\n"]
[4.05, "o", "Title:     \u001b[1mHybrid Local Remote And SSH Execution\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:    \u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m\r\nCreated:   \u001b[2m2026-03-12 06:15:49\u001b[0m\r\nStarted:   \u001b[2m2026-03-12 06:25:27\u001b[0m\r\nUpdated:   \u001b[2m2026-03-12 07:10:35\u001b[0m\r\nCompleted: \u001b[2m2026-03-12 07:10:35\u001b[0m (\u001b[2m45m\u001b[0m)\r\nPath:      \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VDcStPolu/README.md\u001b[0m\r\nPRD:       \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VDcStPolu/PRD.md\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mProblem\u001b[0m\r\n  Port already models remote Linux providers and ships a live hosted control\r\n  plane plus node-agent split, but direct remote SSH usage is still a boundary\r\n  instead of a first-class product surface. The user wants to deploy to the\r\n  cloud and operate across local plus remote environments with first-class SSH.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m: Define one canonical hybrid execution contract for local runtime, hosted control plane, and SSH-first remote Linux ownership. (\u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport\u001b[0m planning artifacts and CLI-facing route or ownership language describe one shared machine and guest model instead of separate local, hosted, and remote vocabularies. -> Epic PRD, voyage SRS/SDD, and downstream stories all preserve one command family with explicit ownership boundaries.)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m: Ship the first executable SSH-first remote Linux workflow through the canonical machine lifecycle surfaces. (A scoped voyage lands \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mmachine launch\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mstatus\u001b[0m, and \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mstop\u001b[0m expectations for a remote Linux host reachable over SSH with proof-backed verification. -> One bounded SSH-first delivery slice is planned and ready for operator execution.)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m: Make remote auth, bootstrap, and readiness explicit for operators before execution begins. (\u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport doctor\u001b[0m, docs, and planning artifacts distinguish local prerequisites from remote-host readiness, auth material, and bootstrap requirements. -> Operators can tell whether a machine targets local runtime, hosted control plane, or SSH-managed remote ownership before launch.)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m: Preserve and extend the existing local and hosted product lanes rather than replacing them. (The epic leaves local Linux and hosted control-plane flows intact and treats SSH as an additional ownership lane, not a compatibility shim or second CLI. -> No planned slice relies on fallback from SSH to local runtime or on a new remote-only command family.)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mScope Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m(no scope drift detected)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mRequirement Coverage\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-01\u001b[39m - Port must model hybrid execution with one canonical host-connection contract that covers local runtime ownership, hosted control-plane ownership, and SSH-first remote Linux ownership.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDeuazAgk\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-02\u001b[39m - Port must support a first scoped SSH-first remote Linux workflow through canonical \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mmachine launch\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mstatus\u001b[0m, and \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mstop\u001b[0m semantics rather than requiring operators to run Port manually on the remote host.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDeuazAgk\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-03\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-03\u001b[39m - Port must surface remote readiness, auth, and bootstrap expectations through \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport doctor\u001b[0m, help text, and operator docs before an SSH-targeted launch begins.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDeuazAgk\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-02\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-04\u001b[39m - Port must keep provider, host, route, and ownership context explicit across local, hosted, and SSH lanes.\r\n    Linked goals (3): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDeuazAgk\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-04\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-05\u001b[39m - Port must publish a proof-backed operator workflow for the hybrid execution contract, including at least one human-reviewable artifact path.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDeuazAgk\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-05\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-01\u001b[39m - Hybrid execution must fail fast with explicit route, host, provider, and ownership detail when a target cannot use the requested lane.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDeuazAgk\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-02\u001b[39m - The SSH-first lane must preserve the shipped local Linux and hosted control-plane workflows without silent behavior changes.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDeuazAgk\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-02\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-03\u001b[39m - Verification for the first hybrid slice must use recommended repo-local techniques, including Rust tests and at least one human-reviewable proof path.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDeuazAgk\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-03\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mPress Release\u001b[0m\r\n  Status:     \u001b[2mnot authored\u001b[0m\r\n  Guidance:   optional; use for large user-facing value shifts\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mProgress\u001b[0m\r\n  Voyages:              1/1 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m1/1\u001b[39m\r\n  Stories:              4/4 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m4/4\u001b[39m\r\n  ETA:                  complete\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Strategy\u001b[0m\r\n  Techniques:\r\n    - Prove hybrid route and lifecycle behavior through story-level Rust tests and\r\n    - Use the proof system for at least one human-reviewable artifact path, such as\r\n    - Validate non-functional posture with explicit failure-path tests, doctor\r\n    - a recording-backed operator workflow for SSH-first launch or diagnostics.\r\n    - proofs, and documented ownership artifacts.\r\n    - repo-local command proofs mapped to voyage requirements.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Readiness\u001b[0m\r\n  Criteria:              automated 16 | manual 0\r\n  Requirement coverage:  automated 8 | manual 0\r\n  Artifact inventory:    text 8 | media 1 | other 1\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVoyages\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDeuazAgk\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - SSH-First Hybrid Execution Foundations (\u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m)\r\n"]
